{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>At Your rebuke</b> — the subject is the Elohim of Jacob, as he mentioned at the beginning: \"In Israel His name is great.\"" "And the meaning of <b>fell asleep</b> — every one of the men of might mentioned in the first verse, and it is: \"every man of might fell asleep, both chariot and horse.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 76, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:43.144921069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}